\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The response must be located in time before its gain is calculated. In the lagged map, the plant advance and control update consume the old pair \((m_k,\theta _k)\). In the post-observation map, the plant advances first and its new state enters the response-driven update. The maps are Eqs.~\eqref  {hrec:eq:lagged} and \eqref  {hrec:eq:post}, respectively. Neither path is an elimination of the other.}}{3}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
